            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a grudge, then the Telugu for contempt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఆనందించు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆనందించు — ānandiñcu — \"to enjoy; to rejoice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సెలవుల్లో పిల్లలు సముద్రం దగ్గర ఆనందించారు. selavullō pillalu samudraṁ daggara ānandiñcāru. In the holidays the children enjoyed themselves by the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ఆనందించాను, ānandiñcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun is ఆనందం, joy; ఆనందంగా, happily."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆనందించు (ānandiñcu) is built on Sanskrit ānanda, \"happiness\" (CDIAL 1172), from the root nand, with the Telugu verb ending -ఇంచు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
