          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొంగిపోవు — poṅgipōvu — \"to be overjoyed; to swell with pride\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బహుమతి గెలిచినప్పుడు ఆమె పొంగిపోయింది. bahumati gelicinappuḍu āme poṅgipōyindi. When she won the prize, she was overjoyed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): పొంగిపోయాను, poṅgipōyānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొంగు is to boil over, like milk: joy that overflows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొంగిపోవు (poṅgipōvu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4469 lists Telugu poṅgu, \"to bubble up, to boil; to rejoice, to be elated\", with Tamil poṅku; pōvu, \"to go\" (DEDR 4572) ends it."
            }
          ]
        },
