        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పులకించు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పులకించు — pulakiñcu — \"to thrill; to be thrilled\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ పాట విని నా మనసు పులకించింది. ā pāṭa vini nā manasu pulakiñcindi. Hearing that song, my heart thrilled."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): పులకించాను, pulakiñcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of the body or the heart: the hair stands on end with joy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పులకించు (pulakiñcu) is built on Sanskrit pulaka, the hair of the body standing on end, a sign of rapture rather than fear (Monier-Williams); the Telugu ending -ఇంచు makes it a verb."
            }
          ]
        },
